      "explanation": "Compound ‘X’ is copper nitrate, i.e. Cu(NO<sub>3</sub>)<sub>2</sub> is an inorganic\ncompound. On treatment with concentrated H<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub> produces brown\nfumes and gives dark brown ring with FeSO<sub>4</sub>\nin presence of\nconcentrated H<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub>. Chemical reaction is as follows\n<br><br><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kx882tx0/2970b3cb-d909-4dc7-bc49-9d3999a425ba/d4c72b40-5e06-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx882tx1.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1kx882tx0/2970b3cb-d909-4dc7-bc49-9d3999a425ba/d4c72b40-5e06-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx882tx1.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 20th July Morning Shift Chemistry - Practical Organic Chemistry Question 87 English Explanation 1\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1kx882tx0/2970b3cb-d909-4dc7-bc49-9d3999a425ba/d4c72b40-5e06-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx882tx1.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1kx882tx0/2970b3cb-d909-4dc7-bc49-9d3999a425ba/d4c72b40-5e06-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx882tx1.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kx882tx0/2970b3cb-d909-4dc7-bc49-9d3999a425ba/d4c72b40-5e06-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx882tx1.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1kx882tx0/2970b3cb-d909-4dc7-bc49-9d3999a425ba/d4c72b40-5e06-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx882tx1.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1kx882tx0/2970b3cb-d909-4dc7-bc49-9d3999a425ba/d4c72b40-5e06-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx882tx1.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1kx882tx0/2970b3cb-d909-4dc7-bc49-9d3999a425ba/d4c72b40-5e06-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx882tx1.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">\n<br><br>Cu<sup>2+</sup>\nis a group II cation with group II reagents\n(HCl/H<sub>2</sub>S)\n, it gives black coloured precipitates. These precipitates\ngives blue colour solution on treatment with HNO<sub>3</sub>\nfollowed by\nexcess of NH<sub>4</sub>OH.\n<br><br><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kx885zdb/1c22ec49-f45a-44d2-9147-87f806ee37fb/2c6aedf0-5e07-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx885zdc.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1kx885zdb/1c22ec49-f45a-44d2-9147-87f806ee37fb/2c6aedf0-5e07-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx885zdc.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;max-height: 60vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 20th July Morning Shift Chemistry - Practical Organic Chemistry Question 87 English Explanation 2\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1kx885zdb/1c22ec49-f45a-44d2-9147-87f806ee37fb/2c6aedf0-5e07-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx885zdc.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1kx885zdb/1c22ec49-f45a-44d2-9147-87f806ee37fb/2c6aedf0-5e07-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx885zdc.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kx885zdb/1c22ec49-f45a-44d2-9147-87f806ee37fb/2c6aedf0-5e07-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx885zdc.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1kx885zdb/1c22ec49-f45a-44d2-9147-87f806ee37fb/2c6aedf0-5e07-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx885zdc.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1kx885zdb/1c22ec49-f45a-44d2-9147-87f806ee37fb/2c6aedf0-5e07-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx885zdc.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1kx885zdb/1c22ec49-f45a-44d2-9147-87f806ee37fb/2c6aedf0-5e07-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx885zdc.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">"
